  "text_md": "history\n\n***th***\n\n## SA Army observes the 96 anniversary of Armistice Day\n\n##### By CO Marumo Machete,\n\n##### SO3 External Communication\n\n##### SA Army\n\n##### Photos by Lance Bombardier\n\n##### Refilwe Sebopa\n\nemories of Armistice Day of 96 years ago were relived at the SA Army Headquarters in Pretoria as the Chief of\n\n# Mthe SA Army, Lt Gen\n\nVusi Masondo, led the SA Army in marking International Remembrance Day.\n\nContinuing a commemorative tradition that spans more than nine decades, a salvo from the Artillery’s G1 gun opened the proceedings with a deafening bang for the sombre remembrance of the survivors and those that laid down their lives during the war that lasted four years from 1914 until the armistice in 1918.\n\nA two-minute silence was observed, a minute for the survivors of the carnage of World War I and another for those who paid the ultimate sacrifice and perished during the war. This culminated in the last salvo fired by the G1 gun.\n\nThe Chief of the SA Army laid a wreath at the memorial on the*ABOVE: Lt Gen Vusi Masondo, the Chief of the SA Army, laid a* lawns of the SA Army Headquarters*wreath at the memorial on the lawns of the SA Army Headquarters* complex before delivering his tribute.*complex before delivering his tribute.*\n\nAddressing the Army Council and the Generals and spectators in\n\n|attendance, Lt Gen Masondo urged|and remember the warriors of the|to the South African soldiers who|\n|---|---|---|\n|those in attendance never to take for granted the selfless sacrifices made|Great War.”|died pursuing peace and stability on the African continent following the|\n|by those who were involved in the|He continued: “Let us honour their|country’s post-1994 readmission to|\n|war.|sacrifice and strive for a peaceful world where no innocent blood|the international community.|\n|Lt Gen Masondo said: “As the SA|will have to be spilled, as there|In assessing the salient issues|\n|Army marches into its third decade|are so many forms of recourse to|facing our country, the Chief of the|\n|of defending our democracy, let us|avert war and prevent conflict from|SA Army took the opportunity to|\n|join the world as it pauses to reflect|escalating.” He also paid homage|acknowledge the great contribution|\n\n**2 0 1 5 V O L 2 2 N O 1**•**S A S O L D I E R**\n",
